    "context": "Mounting a bucket using s3fs \n\nApplications that expect to read and write to a NFS-style filesystem can use s3fs, which can mount a bucket as directory while preserving the native object format for files.\nThis allows you to interact with your cloud storage using familiar shell commands, like ls for listing or cp to copy files, as well as providing access to legacy applications that rely on reading and writing from local files. For a more detailed overview, [visit the project's official README](https://github.com/s3fs-fuse/s3fs-fuse).\nLooking for instructions for how to use IBM Cloud® Object Storage in an IBM Cloud Kubernetes Service cluster?\no the [bucket's location](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/cloud-object-storage/basics?topic=cloud-object-storage-endpoints). The credentials_file is the file created with the API key or HMAC credentials.\nNow, ls <mountpoint> will list the objects in that bucket as if they were local files (or in the case of object prefixes, as if they were nested directories).\n Performance optimization \n\n\nchmod 0600 <credentials_file>\n\n\n\nNow you can mount a bucket using:\n\ns3fs <bucket> <mountpoint> -o url=http{s}://<endpoint> –o passwd_file=<credentials_file>\n\n\n\nIf the credentials file only has an API key (no HMAC credentials), you'll need to add the ibm_iam_auth flag as well:\n\ns3fs <bucket> <mountpoint> -o url=http{s}://<endpoint> –o passwd_file=<credentials_file> -o ibm_iam_auth\n\n\n\nThe <bucket> in the example refers to an existing bucket and the <mountpoint> is the local path where you want to mount the bucket.",
    "statements": [
        "Create a credentials file containing an API key or HMAC credentials.",
        "Restrict the permissions of the credentials file by running `chmod 0600 <credentials_file>`.",
        "Mount the existing bucket at a local mountpoint using the bucket endpoint by running `s3fs <bucket> <mountpoint> -o url=http{s}://<endpoint> -o passwd_file=<credentials_file>`.",
        "Add `-o ibm_iam_auth` to the S3fs mount command if the credentials file contains only an API key and no HMAC credentials.",
        "After mounting the bucket, run `ls <mountpoint>` to list the bucket objects as local files.",
        "Object prefixes appear as nested directories in the mounted bucket."
    ]
}
